+      "utf8_text": "# Embedded method implementation handoff\n\nScope: `23` assigned Skills audited at `5f442723e95fa7ca846b7c3ddc9f9995c7a27065`; `45` actual read paths matched against baseline Git blobs. Initial decisions and source hashes are in `audit-embedded.json`. The initial `preserve` decision for performance profiling does not preclude the root integrator's separate loaded-artifact identity change.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `skills/adk-register-map-design/SKILL.md`: distinguish documented undefined reset bits/conditional reset from missing evidence; resolve effective SVD reset value/mask and inherited conditions; compare only known bits after the whole access is established read-safe; zero comparable bits remain not-testable. Entry `3920 → 3898` UTF-8 bytes.\n- `skills/adk-protocol-stack-integration/SKILL.md`: direct conditional link and output field for transport/framing/buffer/partial-I/O evidence. Entry `3838 → 4029` bytes.\n- `skills/adk-protocol-stack-integration/references/transport-boundaries.md`: separate stream framing/partial sends/receive EOF from datagram empty/truncation semantics; preserve deadline/backpressure, length limits, session boundaries and project APIs. No protocol framework or target-device operation.\n- `tests/test_skill_domain_execution.py`: extract the actual reset expression from the published Markdown, compile native C and execute six independent nonzero-mask examples. Required native compiler fails under GitHub Actions if missing; local missing tools are explicit skip.\n\nNo manifest, catalog, global version, shared test shell or existing test was edited by this agent. Root must wire `tests.test_skill_domain_execution` into the existing content test entry. No commit/push was performed.\n\n## Actual checks\n\n- `embedded-audit-probes.py` and `embedded-audit-probes.json`: four real native Linux AF_UNIX socketpair observations (short header, two frames in one receive, empty datagram followed by a live message, MSG_TRUNC with discarded remainder); each socket has a one-second bound. One synthetic mask arithmetic observation is explicitly not hardware/SVD-generator evidence.\n- `embedded-skill-regression.log`: existing content, portfolio and trigger modules, `39 tests`, success. This ran before the final entry compression; root's final full regression remains required.\n- `embedded-targeted.log`: final reset expression plus existing fake-register/tool-boundary check, `2 tests`, success.\n- `git diff --check`: final success.\n\n## Preserved failed iteration\n\nThe first new inline reset expression was `(observed ^ expected) & known_mask == 0`. Root identified that C/C++ binds `==` before `&`. The real C regression then failed with `case 0: actual=0 expected=1` (`embedded-reset-red.log`, exit 1). This was introduced during this implementation, not a pre-existing ADK runtime bug.\n\nCorrected expression: `((observed ^ expected) & known_mask) == 0`. The same six-vector test passes (`embedded-reset-green.log`, exit 0). The test extracts the published expression instead of maintaining a separate implementation of it. The original failing complete Skill snapshot was not captured; this note preserves the exact expression, raw test log and test source, without claiming a frozen source SHA for that intermediate run.\n\n## Primary sources checked\n\n- https://open-cmsis-pack.github.io/svd-spec/latest/elem_special.html — `turn9view0`, registerPropertiesGroup, defined/undefined bits and inheritance. Both search engines were used to verify the official source.\n- https://docs.python.org/3.12/howto/sockets.html — `turn9view2`, partial stream I/O and frame boundaries; Python 3.12.16 rendered documentation.\n- https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/recv.2.html — `turn14view0`, MSG_TRUNC, empty datagram, zero-size request and stream EOF. Rendered Linux man-pages `6.19`, `recv(2)` date `2025-10-29`.\n- The Open Group 2024 recvmsg page returned 403; no claim is based on an unread page.\n\nNo third-party prose or code was copied. These are reference-based method changes. No model A/B, provider-token/cost reduction, network-service operation, MCU stack, target board, hardware reset, MMIO or HIL result is claimed.\n\n## Original profile budget refinement\n\nRoot's first profile check rejected the aggregate new content (`profile-first-check.json`). This agent compressed redundant entry prose and reduced the new transport reference to five conditional steps, preserving actual acquisition authorization, target distinctions, deadline/Retry-After semantics, capture/error provenance, protocol counterexamples and non-pass gaps. No profile limit was changed.\n\nFinal domain bytes: register entry `3920 → 3856` (`-64`); protocol entry `3838 → 3060` (`-778`); new transport reference `1135`. Combined entries/resources `7758 → 8051`, net `+293` bytes, down from the initial `+2783`. These are UTF-8 source bytes, not measured model tokens or costs. The existing timing/retry contract stays in the main entry; the new I/O details load only for send/receive work.\n\nFinal checks run after compression are recorded separately in `embedded-final-regression.log`; the earlier logs and metrics above describe their original iterations.\n"
